#
# creating locales is optional (POSIX2_LOCALEDEF): these tests report NOTINUSE
# when the system does not claim it.

assertion  XBD.7.1-locale-general.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.1
class      required
since      1992
says       When a locale environment variable names a locale by a pathname
           beginning with a slash, setlocale() selects the locale definition
           made at that pathname by localedef.
timeout    120
test       t/001-pathname-in-lc-all.c

assertion  XBD.7.1-locale-general.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.1
class      required
since      2008
says       newlocale() with the empty name takes the locale from the
           environment, and with LC_ALL naming the pathname of a locale made
           by localedef the object carries that locale.
timeout    120
test       t/002-pathname-with-newlocale.c
